  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Training for Peace Phase VI</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Expected results of the programmet is to contribute to the enhanced capacity of the African Union Commission (AUC) and its collaborative partners to prevent, manage and resolve conflicts and promote stability in Africa. 
The TfP programme will seek to achieve the following key outcomes (effects on the target group) in partnership with the AUC:
Cluster 1: Staff at AUC and REC/RM strategic headquarters have knowledge on the most current realities in PSOs in Africa and the policies and capacities to influence strategic decision makers to ensure effective deployments and enhance performance of deployed personnel in AU PSOs.
Cluster 2: Processes and structures for inclusive and resilient conflict prevention, stabilisation and governance institutions are strengthened at the AUC and RECs/RMs to support enhancement of the capacity of governance institutions in Member States, in building resilience and adaptive systems for  sustainable conflict prevention, peace consolidation and stabilisation.
Cluster 3: Strategic thinking and partnerships at the AUC respond effectively to new and existing global, regional and national dynamics and actors through the delineation of roles and responsibilities between relevant pPartners that facilitate coherence and help to achieve complementarity.</narrative>
  </description>
